Your first message:

> I downloaded your OCT system to have a look at it.  It looks
> very slick.  Just a quick question, does the NeXT ObjC compiler
> make use of a prelinker ?  Does it also need startup initialization
> of classes ?  Just curious...

I don't believe the NeXT system requires any prelinking.  However,
for ultimate copmatibility with any system, I _do_ have a prelinker.
It merely constructs a list of class control blocks to inspect
upon startup.  Most of these describe classes, so that is how I find
out the classes included.  Othertimes, it just describes a module
with routines in it (ie, main.m).  For both cases, the array of
unimplemented selectors must be "bound" in (resolved).  To bind,
the selector names are converted into unique values (SEL's).
See file methods/subbind.c for details.

On the NeXT, upon startup of the application, each class recieves
the message "initialize."

If you are serious about this stuff, I recommend either Dr. Cox's
"object oriented programming: an evolutionary apoproach", 2ed,
or the NeXT documentation set, about $130US.


