Currently, I', working on improving the grammar.  Seems that if
you try:

@interface Foo : Object
{
	int    xxx, yyy;
}
- doit;
@end

@implementation Foo

- doit
{
      myfunc( xxx, yyy, self );
}
@end

Then 'yyy' won't be noticed as an instance variable, even though 'xxx'
will be correctly translated.  The call to myfunc() should be:
	myfunc( (self->xxx), (self->yyy), self );

